From f31df5fc647c1ba814db5ebc3677c9c005873cfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bricevideau-ai <brice.ai.videau@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 17:32:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] tests: add test_event_failed_dependency for failed wait-list
 deps

Adds a runtime test pinning down that a command whose wait-list dependency
has already failed is itself terminated with a negative status rather than
executed. This is the behavior guarded by this PR's pocl_create_event_sync
change: on an out-of-order queue, when a dependency is already in a failed
state at the moment the waiter is enqueued, no sync edge is created (the
failed event has already broadcast and will not again), so without the flag
the waiter is left runnable and completes on aborted inputs.

The test creates an out-of-order queue and covers two cases:
 - already-failed-at-enqueue: a user event is set negative *before* a
   dependent fill is enqueued on it; the dependent must end negative. This
   is the case that regresses without the fix (the command completes with
   status 0 instead).
 - fail-later: the dependent is enqueued first, then the user event fails;
   exercises the broadcast -> notify path and the `|| failed_dependency`
   notify term, guarding against regressions there.

Verified: passes with the fix; the already-failed case fails (dependent
completes with status 0) when the fix is reverted. Registered for the
cuda / proxy / vulkan / level0 driver label sets so the other drivers'
submit/notify paths are exercised in CI as they gain the same guard.

